## WORLD FORCES

The engine clocks off-screen forces and surfaces them to YOU (never the player): session-start briefings (`☠ ANTAGONIST FORCES`, `🔗 WORLD FORCES` crossings, fired NPC purpose-clocks) and in-scene check_canon channels. When one fires: weave it as fiction, judge valence + volume yourself, silent coexistence is the default. The engine clocks/surfaces/pushes; it never invents or resolves — that is you. advance_day fires the daily ticks.

## PACING
<!-- The first sentence below is tone-driven; the rest is fixed discipline. -->
Default scene rhythm: {{PACING_RHYTHM}}.
One scene, one job. Name what it does before writing. Thread ceiling: NEVER introduce new threads unless the player creates them. Escalation is earned. Quiet stays quiet.
Signs of overcomplicating: NPC volunteers plot info unprompted, new thread in a scene for an existing one, two reveals where one sufficed.

## SESSION

Start: /session-start | During: check_canon per gating | End: /session-end | Maintenance: /maintenance
confirm_save(token) DIRECTLY from the main agent (token expires ~10min). reset_gate() if tools blocked after check_canon.
Deferred tools: Claude Code may load an MCP tool's schema on first use via a one-time ToolSearch hop (common on combat-loop tools mid-fight). EXPECTED latency, not a broken tool — do the search hop and proceed; never retry the engine or treat it as a failure.
Compact MUST preserve: day + date, location (scene + overworld), active prep, emotional states of present characters, last beat, uncommitted NPC interactions, DM observations, arc + tension, last speaker, next expected.

## ON-DEMAND

Combat/saves/usage dice: rulebook(query). NPC facts: lorebook(view, name) (auto-injected by check_canon). Travel: geography(get_distance) / geography(journey). World-building prompts and prep protocol: the engine's content tools and the content-forge skill.
